  "description": "The warning signs are getting louder, but price action says its too early to panic.",
  "body_html": "<p>Do not get me wrong… I do think we are in a massive bubble. Huge… And I am not saying the market can’t go down more. However…</p><h4><strong>Until price action shows us a break… we remain in a bull market. </strong></h4><p>Relax. Breathe. </p><p>There are still many great stocks to buy. When a real “blood bath” comes along, there will be a sea of red. </p><h4>Some notes as we start this week:</h4><ol><li><p>Recall when we found Palantir, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$PLTR&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> back in 2024? And have you heard me often reference with stocks like SpaceX, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$SPCX&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> that, “if its a good stock, it will be around in 2-3 years.” Instead of doing Mid-week movers this week, I am going through all of the stocks that had their IPO in 2023 and 2024. There is over 300 of them, so this will take some time. </p><ol><li><p>Speaking of Mid-Week movers, both “recession resistant” stocks remain in a buy range.   <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/the-average-midweek-mover-stock-is?r=4z8lgl\">You can watch last week’s stock rankings here.</a></strong></p><p></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p></li></ol></li><li><p>Oil… I am seeing the $200 a barrel narrative come back into the spotlight. Recall, oil has what is known as Price Elasticity. This is a measure of how consumer’s buying habits change as the price of the service or product changes. An example: the price of beef has risen dramatically. What have people done? Stopped consuming as much beef. The same applies to oil. This is not to say that Oil prices can’t go up more. But these “to the moon” targets are unrealistic. Demand will simply fall off the higher oil prices go. I consider oil trading, to be similar to playing with dynamite. Regardless of local price action, driven by news and erroneous speculation, my macro bearish call for oil remains. </p></li></ol><p>I take Monday’s pretty light, just to let the markets “digest” the weekend news… we had a lot of news this week. I still have <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/the-market-reversed-here-are-my-3?r=4z8lgl\">Stocks I am buying and entry ranges</a> </strong>that remain relevant this week. </p><p>Ignore the news. The best indicator out there is price action itself. Go with trend. I am excited for a bear market, but frankly, I am not seeing any signs of that today. </p><p>If you have questions, feel free to swing by the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/eb3f00e6-9f30-4570-8e48-c0bde66e4eec\">Main Chat</a>. </p><h4>If you like this content, be sure to Re-Stack 🔄 and Like ❤️</h4><p>Thanks for stopping by! </p><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/is-the-ai-bubble-finally-popping?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Know someone into investing? Are they panicking? Share this post with them!</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/is-the-ai-bubble-finally-popping?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/is-the-ai-bubble-finally-popping?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
